  "no_program_found": false,
  "notes": "Alabama's All-State chorus is run by the Alabama Vocal Association (AVA), the choral division of the Alabama Music Educators Association (AMEA), a NAfME state affiliate. AVA labels the season by the spring festival year (\"2027 All-State\"), which is the 2026-27 school year; data on the site was current for that season at retrieval. Five audition choirs (MS Treble, MS Mixed, HS SSAA, HS TTBB, HS SATB) plus a separate All-State Show Choir. Every choir performs the common piece \"Alabama\" in addition to its own repertoire. Note AVA also announced a 2026-2027 trial year in which sight-singing assessments are administered but do not count toward All-State selection (per an AMEA/AVA news post); the AVA All-State pages themselves do not detail that, so it is not encoded as a requirement here.",
  "organization": {
    "name": "Alabama Vocal Association",
    "acronym": "AVA",
    "website_url": "https://alabamavocalassociation.org/",
    "description": "The Alabama Vocal Association is the choral division of the Alabama Music Educators Association (AMEA). It administers statewide choral events including the All-State Choral Festival, the All-State Show Choir Festival, State Choral Performance Assessment, Solo & Ensemble, and Honor Choir."
